@startuml
title Figure 1. ResourceHive System Context
left to right direction
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam ArrowFontSize 12
skinparam nodesep 55
skinparam ranksep 65
skinparam shadowing false
actor "Public Visitor" as Visitor
actor "Approved Member" as Member
actor "Organization Administrator" as OrgAdmin
actor "Platform Administrator" as PlatformAdmin
actor "System Operator" as Operator
rectangle "ResourceHive Platform\nMulti-tenant resource sharing" as RH
cloud "Institutional Email / SMTP Provider" as SMTP
cloud "OAuth Provider\n(provider TBD)" as OAuth
database "PostgreSQL 15-compatible Provider" as DB
cloud "DNS and HTTPS Infrastructure" as DNS
Visitor --> RH : Learn, sign up, log in
Member --> RH : Discover and book resources
OrgAdmin --> RH : Manage hierarchy, members, resources
PlatformAdmin --> RH : Onboard and enforce tenants
Operator --> RH : Configure, deploy, monitor
RH --> SMTP : Verification, reset, notifications
RH --> OAuth : Optional approved social sign-in
RH --> DB : Persistent domain data
RH --> DNS : Public application/API addressing
@enduml


